WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.013
- Before you became
Cedric the Entertainer,

00:00:02.013 --> 00:00:03.840
well, we were all different things, right?

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.450
But, you were Cedric the Claims Adjuster.

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:07.800
- Oh, yeah.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.050
- How'd you end up working in insurance

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:12.470
for a living, and I want to see it.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:13.805
- I worked for State Farm, I worked...

00:00:13.805 --> 00:00:14.638
(laughter)

00:00:14.638 --> 00:00:16.320
- I worked for State Farm, I was uh-

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.153
- Good company, solid company.

00:00:17.153 --> 00:00:19.116
- Yeah, uh, State Farm, uh,
you were in good hands...

00:00:19.116 --> 00:00:20.639
- You were in good hands!

00:00:20.639 --> 00:00:23.643
(laughter)

00:00:23.643 --> 00:00:25.960
- How did you talk to people
about their accidents?

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.690
- Aw, man, I considered myself bilingual,

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:31.230
'cause I spoke regular
English and Angry Negro,

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:32.418
that's what I was there for.

00:00:32.418 --> 00:00:33.251
(laughter)

00:00:33.251 --> 00:00:34.084
- Oh my God!

00:00:34.084 --> 00:00:37.190
- The Black people come in,
they threaten you the most

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:38.415
about they car, like, you know,

00:00:38.415 --> 00:00:40.440
"Oh, you gone fix this right here!"

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.740
Then everybody'd be, like, scared,

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:43.920
and I'm like, "bro, come here,
come here man, lean on it."

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:44.753
- You calm them down?

00:00:44.753 --> 00:00:45.586
- Yeah, bro, you not, that- you-

00:00:45.586 --> 00:00:47.310
people want they cars totaled for

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.220
little to nothing, so
they can get a new car.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:50.053
- Absolutely.

00:00:50.053 --> 00:00:52.520
- But I was a really- I was
not a good claims adjuster,

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:54.566
'cause I was starting my
comedy career at the same time,

00:00:54.566 --> 00:00:56.397
so I would leave people in rental cars

00:00:56.397 --> 00:00:57.771
a very long time, like...

00:00:57.771 --> 00:00:58.930
(laughter)

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:00.350
- Which was good, if you looked like-

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:02.130
wanted to ride around in a cool new car-

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:03.670
somebody might be in a
rental car to this day,

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:04.503
right now, because of me, I'm....

00:01:04.503 --> 00:01:06.566
- Just still waiting, waiting...

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:09.770
- Twenty years riding around like...

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:11.111
in a Malibu.

00:01:11.111 --> 00:01:12.860
- Did you enjoy it?

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:14.329
Because I enjoyed some
of my previous jobs-

00:01:14.329 --> 00:01:15.600
I really liked some of them.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.160
- It was- that actually was a good job,

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.100
because I got, you
know, you had the office

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.580
and then you would get out sometimes,

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.670
'cause you have to go around and

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:23.441
see people, stuff at like, shops,

00:01:23.441 --> 00:01:25.030
to make sure they were working,

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:25.900
so that was fun.

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:28.910
But then, I sold equipment, I mean,

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:30.589
like, electronics for Best Buy

00:01:30.589 --> 00:01:31.547
- Oh my gosh!

00:01:31.547 --> 00:01:32.380
- at one point in time...

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:33.213
- Another great company.

00:01:33.213 --> 00:01:34.046
- Oh...

00:01:34.046 --> 00:01:34.879
- I get lost in that store.

00:01:34.879 --> 00:01:36.000
- But, the job- job- the job that was-

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.504
I was most embarrassed I was in the do-

00:01:37.504 --> 00:01:39.160
I had graduated from college,

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.651
but I didn't get a job right away,

00:01:40.651 --> 00:01:42.490
and I had a paper route, I threw

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:44.230
the Wall Street Journal, and so...

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:45.063
- Oh my gosh!

00:01:45.063 --> 00:01:45.896
I actually think that's so...

00:01:45.896 --> 00:01:46.729
- You did?

00:01:46.729 --> 00:01:47.770
- Like, nostalgic and endearing, like,

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:48.990
a paper boy, that's cool!

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:51.310
- Yeah, but I was grown, I was, like, 27.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:52.156
- Oh!

00:01:52.156 --> 00:01:53.614
(laughter)

00:01:53.614 --> 00:01:54.531
- Not cute.

00:01:56.356 --> 00:01:57.920
It was not, uh...

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:59.750
- I actually- I forgot
to put that together

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:01.386
- Yeah, yeah exactly!

00:02:01.386 --> 00:02:02.219
What, I'm like, on my
little brother's bike...

00:02:02.219 --> 00:02:05.910
- So you're like, a grown man...

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:08.280
- But my mother was, like,
not payin' my car insurance,

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:09.113
so I had to get the money from somewhere,

00:02:09.113 --> 00:02:09.946
- You were like, I gotta do it.

00:02:09.946 --> 00:02:10.779
- So, I was like, (vocalizing)

00:02:10.779 --> 00:02:12.470
- I've had a lot of jobs that I didn't

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:13.680
particularly love, either, but...

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:14.513
- What you do?

00:02:14.513 --> 00:02:15.346
What kind of stuff?

00:02:15.346 --> 00:02:16.330
- Oh my gosh, I've done everything.

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:18.371
I have sold vac- well,
for one day, I trained,

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:20.928
and then I sold Kirby
vacuum cleaners for one day,

00:02:20.928 --> 00:02:23.360
because I was like, what?

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:24.660
Like, we just throw dirt

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.330
on someone's floor, and
the man was not happy,

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:27.630
I left, I went to a gas station,

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:29.100
and my friend picked me up, I worked-

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.230
actually, I was a cocktail waitress

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:31.530
at a comedy club for years, Hyenas,

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.913
I worked at a pizza joint, Papa John's,

00:02:33.913 --> 00:02:34.746
- Nice.

00:02:34.746 --> 00:02:35.910
- I've worked everywhere, you can- zoos,

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:36.873
I've worked everywhere.

00:02:36.873 --> 00:02:37.890
- You worked at the zoo?

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.100
- I worked at the zoo,
and here's the thing,

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:40.880
I was so excited about it, but Texas heat,

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:41.952
that's not real fun, right?

00:02:41.952 --> 00:02:42.785
- Oh...

00:02:42.785 --> 00:02:44.040
- And so, you're outside, and I was new,

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:45.300
and they put me by the monkeys,

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:48.470
what- so, I was like,
"that's so adorable!"

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:49.810
And then I got there, and the

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:51.400
whole place just smells like monkey poo,

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:52.233
the whole time.

00:02:52.233 --> 00:02:53.066
- Yeah.

00:02:53.066 --> 00:02:53.950
- I'm just breathing in-

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:54.899
- And they will throw it at you-

00:02:54.899 --> 00:02:55.732
- Monkey feces.

00:02:55.732 --> 00:02:56.565
- You know, monkeys will..

00:02:56.565 --> 00:02:57.398
- Yeah!

00:02:57.398 --> 00:02:58.320
I wasn't that close, but...

00:02:58.320 --> 00:02:59.280
- Monkeys will throw
it at you, you know...

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.243
- I do love the zoo, though,

00:03:00.243 --> 00:03:01.076
- Yeah.

00:03:01.076 --> 00:03:01.989
- I think the zoo is
awesome, but, anyway...

00:03:01.989 --> 00:03:02.822
- Oh, that's nice.

00:03:02.822 --> 00:03:04.430
- We heard you left State Farm, though,

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:06.280
without a final performance review.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:07.770
So, obviously, we wanted to clean

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:08.930
this up for you, right?

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:12.150
So, we invited your old
boss, Daryl Anderson,

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:13.260
to take care of that.

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:14.430
Where's Daryl?

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:16.808
(laughter)

00:03:16.808 --> 00:03:19.191
(cheering)

00:03:19.191 --> 00:03:20.024
- Classic!

00:03:20.024 --> 00:03:21.162
- So,

00:03:21.162 --> 00:03:22.394
- Aw, that's awesome.

00:03:22.394 --> 00:03:26.260
- Daryl, what was Cedric
like around the office?

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.480
- When we interviewed Cedric, I mean,

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:29.970
he came in with so much energy,

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:32.080
he was so comfortable talking with people,

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:33.460
we knew he'd be a great fit, so,

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:35.180
we had no problem bringing him in.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:36.449
- Oh, you were a joy!

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:37.690
- Yeah, I was good, see that!

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:40.360
- Okay, well, would you like to finally

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:42.270
give Cedric that performance review?

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:43.438
Because I'd like you to.

00:03:43.438 --> 00:03:44.290
- Okay.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.410
- Okay, okay- on a scale of one to five,

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:49.200
Daryl, how was he at customer service?

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.770
'Cause somebody's maybe still driving

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:52.701
around in a Malibu, so keep that in mind.

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:55.780
- Uh, you know, I would give him a five,

00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:58.160
simply because he worked
in a tough environment,

00:03:58.160 --> 00:03:59.390
where there were people coming in,

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:00.650
and most of the time people weren't happy

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:03.516
when they came in, and
after they talked to Cedric,

00:04:03.516 --> 00:04:05.796
they always left with
a smile, so probably...

00:04:05.796 --> 00:04:06.671
- Oh, that's good!

00:04:06.671 --> 00:04:07.504
- See?

00:04:07.504 --> 00:04:08.719
- It's all great.

00:04:08.719 --> 00:04:12.940
All right, on a scale
of one to five, Daryl,

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:15.730
how was he at getting
customers in and out?

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:20.390
- Um, well, I mean, I
probably would give him

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:24.361
a one on that, and that was only because

00:04:24.361 --> 00:04:26.570
I don't think he missed an opportunity

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:28.519
to work on a routine or some of his jokes.

00:04:28.519 --> 00:04:29.483
- Yes!

00:04:29.483 --> 00:04:30.720
- So he'd keep people a little bit longer

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:31.553
than they needed to be there.

00:04:31.553 --> 00:04:32.960
- I talk a lot, too, I get it.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:33.793
- Yeah.

00:04:33.793 --> 00:04:34.626
- Do you agree with that?

00:04:34.626 --> 00:04:35.459
Were you kind of a-

00:04:35.459 --> 00:04:36.320
- Yeah, that's a pretty good assessment,

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:38.620
because we would also
have these little rooms,

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:40.360
where you go and try to talk to people,

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:42.010
and, once you get somebody in there,

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.533
you can just, like, "where you from?"

00:04:43.533 --> 00:04:44.950
You know, like...

00:04:45.917 --> 00:04:47.820
"You know what, my cousin
went to that school."

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:51.068
And so, you know, you off and...

00:04:51.068 --> 00:04:51.962
- You just start to- you just-

00:04:51.962 --> 00:04:52.853
- Yeah, you're just like...

00:04:52.853 --> 00:04:53.686
- you distract them.

00:04:53.686 --> 00:04:54.519
That's how you discract...

00:04:54.519 --> 00:04:55.352
- And I would have- and I would definitely

00:04:55.352 --> 00:04:57.820
have files, he could tell you this, too,

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:00.170
because, I would just let stuff pile up,

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:01.560
because I did comedy at night,

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:04.878
so I would come in to
work, just, dog tired,

00:05:04.878 --> 00:05:07.300
so, it would be days,
where it would just be

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:08.880
claims just piled up on my desk.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:10.790
And he would have to get other people

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:13.170
to come help me like,
kind of service my claims.

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:14.003
People be callin' and I-

00:05:14.003 --> 00:05:14.836
- Well, Daryl was nice.

00:05:14.836 --> 00:05:15.669
- And I hadn't got to them.

00:05:15.669 --> 00:05:16.502
Daryl was great.

00:05:16.502 --> 00:05:17.335
- Daryl was nice!

00:05:17.335 --> 00:05:18.467
- You was great, my man.

